  "name": "HEPATITIS B  SURFACE ANTIGEN (HBSAG) CONFIRMATORY ASSAY",
  "code": "2763",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.028%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 49.9303%;\"><col style=\"width: 49.9303%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Result</span></strong></td>\n<td><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Remarks</span></strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Confirmed</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Sample is positive for HbsAg</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Non -&nbsp; Confirmed</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Sample is negative for HbsAg</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Note</span></strong><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">1. Confirmed test result indicates sample is positive for HBsAg as it could neutralize the anti -HBsAg in the assay.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">2. Not-Confirmed test result indicates sample is negative for HBsAg as it could not neutralize the anti-HBsAg in the assay.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">3. False positive results may be observed in patients receiving mouse monoclonal antibodies, on heparin therapy, on biotin</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">supplements for diagnosis or therapy, presence of heterophilic antibodies in serum or after HBV vaccination for transient </span><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">period of time.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">4. False negative reaction may be due to processing of sample collected early in the course of disease or presence of </span><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">mutant forms of HBsAg</span></p>",
